Subject: dialog-v2: a fitted dialog grows with its content up to a maximum

What: `fit` comes after the size rules, so it also applies to `large` and `x-large`
dialogs, and it bounds the card by a maximum height instead of dropping the
bound: a fitted card is as tall as its content, up to its size's height (368 px
normal, 480 px large, 600 px x-large), and scrolls inside past that. A caller
sets another maximum through `--dialog-v2-fit-max-height` on the container
(`containerClass`).
Why: the size rules came after `fit` with the same specificity, so a
`fit size="large"` dialog kept the fixed 480 px height and `fit` did nothing
there, and a fitted dialog's only bound was the viewport. A palette with two
matching rows drew a 480 px card with a mostly empty area under them. The
original generation's list and form dialogs fitted their content inside a
640x512 box; the long forms keep that 512 px maximum through the property.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/dialog-v2.css b/src/v2/components/dialog-v2.css
index 79892dfa28..53470c889d 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/dialog-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/dialog-v2.css
@@ -155,16 +155,6 @@
     }
   }
 
-  &[data-fit] {
-    .ui-dialog-container {
-      height: auto;
-
-      .ui-dialog-content {
-        min-height: 0;
-      }
-    }
-  }
-
   &[data-size="large"] .ui-dialog-container {
     width: min(calc(100vw - 32px), 640px);
     height: min(calc(100vh - 32px), 480px);
@@ -179,4 +169,23 @@
     width: min(calc(100vw - 64px), 1400px);
     height: calc(100vh - 64px);
   }
+
+  &[data-fit] {
+    .ui-dialog-container {
+      height: auto;
+      max-height: var(--dialog-v2-fit-max-height, min(calc(100vh - 16px), 368px));
+
+      .ui-dialog-content {
+        min-height: 0;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
+  &[data-fit][data-size="large"] .ui-dialog-container {
+    max-height: var(--dialog-v2-fit-max-height, min(calc(100vh - 32px), 480px));
+  }
+
+  &[data-fit][data-size="x-large"] .ui-dialog-container {
+    max-height: var(--dialog-v2-fit-max-height, min(calc(100vh - 92px), 600px));
+  }
 }
